    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 the full suite (the one `AcceptanceTest`) passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a server-derived `checkDigit` \u2014 the Luhn check digit over the digits of `customerCode` \u2014 following the codebase's existing pattern for derived owner fields (`membershipNumber`, `locality`, etc.).\n\nThree small, cohesive changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `checkDigit` property (integer 0\u20139, readOnly) to the `Owner` schema, right after `customerCode`, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`CheckDigit.java`** (new) \u2014 a one-method helper class mirroring `MembershipNumber`, implementing the exact Luhn algorithm the acceptance test uses.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` expression wiring `CheckDigit.of(owner.getCustomerCode())` into `toOwnerDto`, so every owner response (GET and POST) carries the field automatically.\n\nThis keeps structural impact low: the algorithm lives in its own new class (no surrounding complexity), the only edited existing method (`toOwnerDto`) is an abstract interface method with minimal context, and no responder, endpoint YAML, or entity code had to change.",
